            text: "Because nothing changes unless you change it. Outdoors, corners, hills, traffic and scenery break a run into small events; on a treadmill the pace, view and surface stay identical, so your attention goes to the clock. Treadmill runs also tend to be hotter with no breeze, which makes the same effort feel harder.",
          },
        },
        {
